<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ploiești</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ploiești is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bucharest">Bucharest</a>, at the centre of the Prahova oil region. From the late 19th century it became the hub of the Romanian oil industry, with refineries that made it one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s main sources of petroleum. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> its refineries supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and were heavily bombed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, notably in the American raid of August 1943.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ploiesti.jpg" alt="Ploiești" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Razvan Socol · CC BY-SA 3.0 ro · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casa_Luca_Elefterescu,_azi_Muzeul_Ceasului_%22Nicolae_Simache%22_(2).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
